  "name": "advancing-cold-roll-bonding-efficiency-by-preceding-xhv-adequate-laser-deoxidation",
  "notes": "# Surface Roughness and Critical Deformation Dataset\r\n\r\nThis supplementary Dataset contains experimental data related to surface roughness measurements and critical deformation analysis for cold roll bonding (CRB) processes under extreme high vacuum-adequate (XHV-adequate) conditions. The data supports research on laser-induced surface modifications and their impact on bond formation between aluminum EN AW-1050 and oxygen-free copper (OFC) sheets.\r\n\r\n# Data Structure\r\n\r\n```\r\n├── roughness/                   # Original Excel and csv format\r\n│   ├── new_Analyse_Al_20x_Messung der Oberflächenrauheit_edit.xlsx\r\n│   ├── new_Analyse_Al_20x_Messung der Oberflächenrauheit_edit.csv\r\n│   └── new_Analyse_Cu_20x_Messung der Oberflächenrauheit_edit.xlsx\r\n│   └── new_Analyse_Cu_20x_Messung der Oberflächenrauheit_edit.csv\r\n└── critical_deformation/        # Original Excel  and csv format\r\n    └── crit_deformation_Data.xlsx\r\n    └── crit_deformation_Data.csv\r\n```\r\n\r\n# Dataset Description\r\n\r\nThe dataset is available in both original Excel format and open-access CSV format for maximum accessibility and reusability.\r\n\r\n\r\n## Surface Roughness Measurements\r\nLocated in `/roughness/` directory:\r\n\r\n- `new_Analyse_Al_20x_Messung der Oberflächenrauheit_edit.xlsx/.csv`: Surface characterization of aluminum EN AW-1050 specimens\r\n  - CLSM measurements at 20x magnification\r\n  - Surface roughness parameters (Sa, Sz)\r\n  - Surface topography data for different laser overlap settings (0%, 20%, 40%, 60%)\r\n  - Laser treatment parameters: 180 μJ pulse energy, 700 kHz PRF, 44 μm spot size\r\n\r\n- `new_Analyse_Cu_20x_Messung der Oberflächenrauheit_edit.xlsx/.csv`: Surface characterization of oxygen-free copper specimens\r\n  - CLSM measurements at 20x magnification\r\n  - Surface roughness parameters (Sa, Sz)\r\n  - Surface topography data for different laser overlap settings (0%, 20%, 40%, 60%)\r\n  - Laser treatment parameters: 400 μJ pulse energy, 510 kHz PRF, 35 μm spot size\r\n\r\n## Critical Deformation Analysis\r\nLocated in `/critical_deformation/` directory:\r\n\r\n- `crit_deformation_Data.xlsx/.csv`: Critical reduction data for bond formation\r\n  - Critical deformation values for different surface treatments\r\n  - Comparison between laser-treated (0.5% minimum) and brushed surfaces (19%)\r\n  - Data for sigmoid fitting analysis\r\n  - Process conditions under XHV-adequate atmosphere (pO2 < 10^-15 Vol.-%)\r\n\r\n# Experimental Conditions\r\n\r\n- Material thickness: 1 mm for both Al and Cu sheets\r\n- Atmosphere: Argon-monosilane mixture for XHV-adequate conditions\r\n- Rolling speed: 0.02 m/s\r\n- Roll diameter: 65 mm\r\n\r\n\r\n# Key Findings\r\n\r\nThe dataset demonstrates:\r\n- Significant reduction in critical deformation (εcrit) from 19% (brushed) to 0.5% (laser-treated)\r\n- Correlation between laser parameters and surface morphology\r\n- Enhanced interfacial behavior in laser-treated specimens\r\n- Synergistic effects between laser surface modification and XHV-adequate conditions\r\n\r\n\r\n# Citation\r\n\r\nWhen using this dataset, please cite:\r\n\r\nBarienti, K., Janthur, F.-L., Heimers, H., Seffer, S., Hermsdorf, J., Herbst, S., Overmeyer, L., Maier, H.J., Nürnberger, F., 2025. Advancing cold roll bonding efficiency by preceding XHV-adequate laser deoxidation. Manufacturing Letters 44, 42–46. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mfglet.2025.03.002\r\n\r\n\r\n# Funding\r\n\r\nThis work was funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation)—Project-ID 394563137 SFB1368. ",
